*For every $R<\infty$ and $\eta>0$, there are deterministic partitions $\mathcal P_n$ of uniformly bounded size such that the following holds. These partitions may depend on the leaf laws, but are chosen before the leaves are sampled. For independent leaves, choose a member $f$ and a member $g$ of the two truncated families, allowing either choice to depend on both leaves. If $P_n$ is conditional expectation onto $\mathcal P_n$, then $$\label{eq:limit-projection-error}
\mathbb E\bigl|\langle f,g\rangle-\langle P_nf,P_ng\rangle\bigr|\le\eta.$$ The same conclusion holds for every deterministic refinement of $\mathcal P_n$ chosen independently of the sampled leaves. Multiplication of the discrepancy by any indicator determined by the leaf pair does not increase the bound.

